    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1218">

                <pb facs="1340" n="1328" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg1328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW 1939/10–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-18T21:00:00+03:00">October 18, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 18—6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3981. Moscow press for October 15 features announcement of complete liberation of
                    Ukraine, leading articles and about half total space being devoted to this
                    achievement and progress of reconstruction there. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pravda</hi> leader refers to Kiev, Kharkov, and Lwow as being in a single
                    and indissoluble family of Soviet Ukrainian cities, thereby confirming previous
                    indications that the Soviet Government has abandoned any thought of returning
                    Lwow to Poland.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
